<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>A reputable carrier will break the cost into four clear components: distance, vehicle size, insurance, and taxes.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>Understanding each element helps you compare offers and guarantees that the price you see is the price you pay.</span></li></ul>

<p><strong>1. Distance</strong> – The carrier calculates a per‑kilometer rate based on the actual route from your pickup location to the destination. Since the trip is 850 km, the distance fee is the largest slice of the quote.</p>

<p><strong>2. Vehicle Size</strong> – Whether you’re moving a compact sedan or a full‑size SUV, the vehicle’s dimensions determine the type of trailer and the driver’s skill level required. Larger cars command a higher base rate, but the fixed‑price model keeps this component locked in.</p>

<p><strong>3. Insurance</strong> – All carriers offer a comprehensive coverage plan that protects against accidents, theft, and weather damage. The insurance cost is quoted upfront and is non‑negotiable, ensuring that your vehicle remains protected throughout the entire route.</p>

<p><strong>4. Taxes</strong> – Local and federal taxes are calculated on the subtotal of the above components. The final figure includes a clear line item for taxes so you know exactly how much you’ll pay.</p>

<p>Obtaining the quote is simple. Most carriers provide an online form or a quick phone call. Fill in your pickup address, destination, vehicle make and model, and the date you’d like to travel.</p>
<p>The system will automatically calculate the four cost components and present you with a single, firm price. Once the quote is issued, it remains unchanged regardless of fuel price fluctuations, traffic delays, or any other variables during the 850 km trip.</p>

